1
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:45,000
Into the Woods is a drama, music, fantasy film directed by James Lapine.

2
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:24,000
In a woods filled with magic and fairy tale characters, a baker and his wife set out
to end the curse put on them by their neighbor, a spiteful witch.

3
00:22:57,000 --> 00:23:03,000
Witch, played by Bernadette Peters.

4
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:42,000
Baker, played by Chip Zien.

5
00:38:15,000 --> 00:38:21,000
Baker's Wife, played by Joanna Gleason.

6
00:45:54,000 --> 00:46:00,000
Narrator/Mysterious Man, played by Tom Aldredge.

7
00:53:33,000 --> 00:53:39,000
Cinderella's Prince/Wolf, played by Robert Westenberg.

8
01:01:12,000 --> 01:01:18,000
Cinderella, played by Kim Crosby.

9
01:08:51,000 --> 01:08:57,000
Into the Woods is a 2014 American musical fantasy film directed by Rob Marshall, with a screenplay by
James Lapine based on his and Stephen Sondheim's 1987 Broadway musical of the same name.

10
01:16:30,000 --> 01:16:36,000
Produced by Walt Disney Pictures, it features an ensemble cast that includes Meryl Streep, Emily Blunt,
James Corden, Anna Kendrick, Chris Pine, Tracey Ullman, Christine Baranski, and Johnny Depp.

11
01:24:09,000 --> 01:24:15,000
The film is centered on a childless couple who set out to end a curse placed on them by a vengeful
witch, and the characters are forced to experience the consequences of their actions.

12
01:31:48,000 --> 01:31:54,000
It is inspired by the Grimm Brothers' fairy-tales of "Little Red Riding
Hood", "Cinderella", "Jack and the Beanstalk", and "Rapunzel".

13
01:39:27,000 --> 01:39:33,000
After several unsuccessful attempts by other studios and producers to adapt the musical to film, Disney announced in
2012 that it was producing an adaptation, with Marshall directing and John DeLuca serving as producer.

14
01:47:06,000 --> 01:47:12,000
Principal photography commenced in September 2013, and took place entirely in
the United Kingdom, including at Shepperton Studios in London.

15
01:54:45,000 --> 01:54:51,000
Into the Woods had its world premiere in New York City on December 8, 2014, and was
released theatrically in the United States on December 25, 2014.

16
02:02:24,000 --> 02:02:30,000
It was commercially successful and received generally positive reviews, receiving praise for its acting performances (particularly
Streep's and Blunt's), visual style, production values, and musical numbers, and criticism for its tone in the final act.

17
02:10:03,000 --> 02:10:09,000
Into the Woods was named one of the top-eleven best films of 2014 by the American Film Institute; the film received three Academy Award nominations, including
a Best Supporting Actress nomination for Streep, and three Golden Globe Award nominations, including Best Motion Picture – Musical or Comedy.

18
02:17:42,000 --> 02:17:48,000
The film explores themes of princess, fairy tale,
prince, little red riding hood, musical.

19
02:25:21,000 --> 02:25:27,000
The tone is emotional.
